      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Poking this feature request again as @{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name} said it might return at a later date way back on August 16, 2023. \n\nIt's now almost 3 years later (April 2026), so I was curious if anything had changed?\n\nVRChat now has 'selfie expression' mode through webcams on PC + cameras on supported iPhone / Android devices now, and that feature left VRC+ back in September 2025.\n\nThough I understand that the main issue with the Quest Pro eye tracking on VRChat standalone was due to the performance hit with the XR management backend / upstream SDK + the cost to develop and maintain it: https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/quest-pro-eye-tracking\n\nhttps://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-17-august-2023/19495\n\nAs if I remember right, it's very difficult to grab the FT data from the Quest Pro if another application is in the foreground (like VRChat). So a background app running on a Quest Pro is usually always blocked from accessing the FT data.\n\nI believe the only way still in 2026 to get FT on standalone VRChat on a Quest Pro is through OSC through external hardware (example: a phone attached to your head or neck), as the internal FT hardware of the Quest Pro is strict with how that face tracking data is accessed (see above).\n\nAnyway, it would be cool to see this feature return one day! :3",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-16T23:46:19.935Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "We know it incurs a performance loss, but to many of us, we feel it's worth it to be able to be more expressive, especially on native Quest harder where there's no other solution to have eye tracking.\n\nIf need be, have it in a closed beta branch that you need to agree to additional terms (basically say \"you know this will cause performance loss and we will not be responsible for that\") to join.",
